            <description><![CDATA[
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, sans-serif; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.45; color: #1d1d1f; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; font-size: 15px; }
  h3 { margin: 14px 0 4px 0; font-size: 13px; }
  ul { margin: 4px 0 8px 18px; padding: 0; }
  li { margin: 2px 0; }
</style>

<h2>What's new in v2.7.8</h2>

<h3>Cleaner DMG installer</h3>
<p>The DMG used to show two icons (the app and a Terminal script), which
was confusing. It now shows a single labeled icon — double-click
<b>Install LangAutoSwitcher</b> and a regular macOS dialog walks you
through the install. No Terminal window, no ambiguity about which icon
to click.</p>

<h3>Under the hood</h3>
<ul>
  <li>The installer is now a small AppleScript-based .app embedded in the DMG,
      signed and notarized like the input method itself.</li>
  <li>The actual LangAutoSwitcher.app is bundled inside the installer's
      Resources so users only see one thing in the DMG window.</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
